      <p>At $24.88/year, the i9 Dream Core works out to about <strong>$2.07/month</strong> — squarely in the budget-VPS bracket, but with a faster single-core profile than most $2/mo boxes. DediRock advertises roughly a 9.23% annual saving on the Plus tier and ~22.91% on the Power tier, reinforcing that the headline value is the entry Core plan. You can verify the live lineup on the official <a href="https://dedirock.com/thei9dream/" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline" rel="noopener" target="_blank">DediRock i9 Dream page</a>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">Storage VPS — RAID 5/6 for backups</h2>
      <p>Alongside the i9 line, DediRock keeps its "Storage Wars" storage VPS running. These plans now sit on <strong>RAID 5 and RAID 6</strong> for greater redundancy and reliability. The range starts at <strong>$12.88/year</strong> for 256 GB storage + 1 GB RAM (1,000 GB monthly bandwidth), up to 2 TB storage + 2 GB RAM at $29.88/year (4,000 GB bandwidth). DediRock is explicit that these are <strong>optimized for backups and large files, not heavy 4K random read/write</strong> — so treat them as bulk storage targets, not primary database disks.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">Pros and Cons</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-6">
        <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-6">
